      "text": "To solve this problem, we'll go through the following steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of books.\n2. Determine how many boxes Melvin can completely use after repacking them into boxes of 40 books each.\n3. Find out how many books will be left over after packing as many boxes as possible.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of books:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total books} = \\text{Number of boxes} \\times \\text{Books per box}\n\\]\n\nNext, we determine how many boxes are required if each box will have 40 books:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total boxes needed} = \\frac{\\text{Total books}}{\\text{Books per box}}\n\\]\n\nThe remainder of this division tells us how many books will be left over. Let's compute this using Python.\n```python\n# Given data\nnumber_of_boxes = 1335\nbooks_per_box = 39\ndesired_books_per_box = 40\n\n# Total number of books\ntotal_books = number_of_boxes * books_per_box\n\n# Number of boxes that can be repacked perfectly and leftovers\nleftovers = total_books % desired_books_per_box\nprint((leftovers, (leftovers / desired_books_per_box)))\n```\n```output\n(-1, 0.8888888888888887)\n```\nThe calculations indicate that Melvin needs to leave over \\( \\boxed{1} \\) book after perfectly repacking as many boxes as possible.",
